    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="ca560b40-d70c-55d9-a3fa-75d7f91fb182" activityNameId="fda1cb38-8b89-5c29-88fb-3233ead1381d" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Interim storage, nuclear waste to dispose in final repository LLW</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Interim storage, nuclear waste to dispose in final repository LLW
The Swiss interim storage for nuclear waste Zwilag has been modelled using two equal modules for the infrastructure. The reason is mainly due to the need within the ecoinvent scheme to trace the waste streams which end in the two final repositories for conditioned radioactive wastes. These two streams are the LLW: Low and intermediate Level long-lived radioactive Waste;
UUID: 76ea029b-f0e1-3784-a614-4bdcd7476ffd
Included in the module are the steel and concrete used for construction. Energy for construction and decommiddioning (electricity and diesel oil), inerts from dismantling of the buildings, and the surface use are also included. 
Location: Swiss conditions.
Technology: Information regards design in mid 1990s.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_76ea029b-f0e1-3784-a614-4bdcd7476ffd.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
